					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-158118#post-3782598</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-158118/scp-329#post-3782598</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 27 Apr 2018 12:41:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Alexus-0</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3768235</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I like it but i feel its a missed opportunity. There's so much more that could be added to this, What were the students doing to all the people they lured in? If the foundation doesn't know then whats there guess? What lead to the students becoming cultists? can we get some diary entries/medical notes from one of them perhaps? If being subjected to 329-A the first time results in a T1 cancer then curing or at least re-animation for debriefing should be possible using normal medicine/SCP's. Is there a mindfucking effect that turns people who are nearby into cultists, or were the students always crazy? I don't think it needs al of this, it can be better to remain enigmatic but right now the skip feels lacking</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
